{"name":"Weapon Bronze","hex":"#b47b27","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"weapon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An instrument of attack or defense in combat or hunting, e.g. most guns, missiles, or swords.","An instrument or other means of harming or exerting control over another."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To equip with a weapon; to arm."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weapon"},{"term":"bronze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A naturally occurring or man-made alloy of copper, usually in combination with tin, but also with one or more other metals.","A reddish-brown colour, the colour of bronze."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of bronze metal.","Having a reddish-brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bronze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Weapon","blocks":[{"text":"A weapon, arm, or armament is any implement or tool that is used to deter, threaten, inflict physical damage, harm, or kill. Weapons are used to increase the efficacy and efficiency of activities such as hunting, crime, law enforcement, self-defense, warfare, or suicide. In a broader context, weapons may be construed to include anything used to gain a tactical, strategic, material, or mental advantage over an adversary or enemy target."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Dangerous_weapons_seized_from_holiday_flights_at_Manchester_Airport.jpg/330px-Dangerous_weapons_seized_from_holiday_flights_at_Manchester_Airport.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weapon"},{"title":"Bronze","blocks":[{"text":"Bronze is an alloy consisting primarily of copper, commonly with about 12–12.5% tin and often with the addition of other metals and sometimes non-metals or metalloids. These additions produce a range of alloys some of which are harder than copper alone or have other useful properties, such as strength, 